{"id": "EUVD-2026-26621", "enisaUuid": "43c5461a-0681-38e2-832f-f91cc8ee6a65", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sync: hci_cmd_sync_queue_once() return -EEXIST if exists\n\nhci_cmd_sync_queue_once() needs to indicate whether a queue item was\nadded, so caller can know if callbacks are called, so it can avoid\nleaking resources.\n\nChange the function to return -EEXIST if queue item already exists.\n\nModify all callsites to handle that.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T14:15:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dfee8da127bafa46530b72347bce3ccae736296d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/799e2e5fbf3f14874b5c6cc289a0dd68b2ca1979", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cfa4f537a056c91ac6c09bc3ab58a4455217df7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ad2ce230b38cd4b3f6732cc609e270461e626e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2969554bcfccb5c609f6b6cd4a014933f3a66dd0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qgvr-5r26-m585", "CVE-2026-43022"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02e77d0f-5d57-3726-bf9b-e7df9f55b7ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "505ea2b295929e7be2b4e1bc86ee31cb7862fb01 <2969554bcfccb5c609f6b6cd4a014933f3a66dd0"}, {"id": "45a57b3b-8211-302f-b743-cd853f1ee28a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "48e2c741-3b83-3684-889c-6f06c65133cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "505ea2b295929e7be2b4e1bc86ee31cb7862fb01 <0ad2ce230b38cd4b3f6732cc609e270461e626e5"}, {"id": "4d6a7a50-377f-3ed2-b271-3e4a4ba4b108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "734b336d-42ad-317f-8891-dbd2dafbc6be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.12"}, {"id": "7e11bc9b-0963-343e-ad0f-91c7